== Hyatt IV

Following the discovery of the intrusion in November, the security and @PR:a teams at the Hyatt got to work
remediating the disaster they had on their hands.

On December 8th, the breach gets mitigated and then formally
#link("https://newsroom.hyatt.com/news-releases?item=123450")[publicly acknowledged]
@hyatt-newsroom-ack
by Hyatt on December 23rd

#aside[What a save guys - GG]

I think its important to note that the breach was hot on the heels of
#link("https://abcnews.com/Technology/hyatt-reveals-data-breach-impacted-250-hotels/story?id=36315368")[other hotel hacks],
@abc-hyatt-hack-2015
including #link("https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/oct/05/donald-trump-hotels-hack-malware-credit-card-data")[Donald Trump's Trump Hotel Collection].
@trump-hotels-hack

So it isn't necessarily an isolated incident - targeted maybe, and we'll get into that, but isolated no.
